  $ 0 arrow.r cal(H)^0 arrow.r cal(G)_w \[ q \] arrow.r \( bb(F)_q^2 \)_R arrow.r 0 $
  with $cal(H)^0$ finite flat of rank $q$. No splitting of this sequence over $R$ is asserted.
  Pass to a finite extension of $R$ over which the generic torsion is split. Its active fiber is a three-dimensional $bb(F)_q$-space with distinguished line $cal(H)_(upright("gen"))^0$. For a fixed $b$-dimensional subspace of the label quotient, the generic subspaces disjoint from that line and mapping onto the label subspace are its graph lifts. They form a torsor under the $b$-dimensional space of maps to the line, so there are $q^b$ of them. A generic subspace containing the line is the unique full inverse image of its label subspace.
