  The constructions $X_0 \, Y_0 \, Z_0$ are therefore operations on the ordinary points of the same full moduli space. We use them as multiset operations on points; no global special-fiber algebraic correspondence is required.
  The operation $X_0$ is the $q$-power Frobenius on full tuples. Indeed its total kernel is the connected $q$-torsion on every block. On the active pair, duality pairs the multiplicative part with the opposite étale part and the étale part with the opposite multiplicative part, so the annihilator of $M_0 \[ q \]$ is exactly the opposite connected part; the pure nonactive pairs have the same property. The total kernel is therefore the kernel of relative Frobenius $F_B : B arrow.r B^(\( q \))$. Naturality of the polarization and Frobenius–Verschiebung duality give
