  $ e_(q^h) #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\(] f^dagger u \, f^dagger v #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\)] = e'_(q^h) #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\(] u \, f f^dagger v #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\)] = 1 \, $
  so the image is isotropic in $G \[ q^h \]$. The endomorphism idempotents split its kernel into conjugate-block parts. If $K_j \, K_(macron(j))$ are the parts in one conjugate pair of height-three blocks, then
