   $ nu_iota \( sigma e \) = - 3 / 2 v \( g \) \, #h(2em) t_(sigma eta) = 1 / 2 - 1 / 3 nu_iota \( sigma e \) = frac(1 + v \( g \), 2) . $ <eq:cm-sign-to-hodge-type>]
  The possible sign in the conjugate parameter $e' = plus.minus sigma e$ has valuation zero. Consequently the entire active space for $sigma eta$ is of type $\( 1 \, 0 \)$ when $v \( g \) = 1$ and of type $\( 0 \, 1 \)$ when $v \( g \) = - 1$. This applies to all of its vectors, not just to theta vectors. At the identity it gives type $\( 1 \, 0 \)$, in agreement with $v \( 1 \) = 1$ and the holomorphy of the theta class.
  Each active space is defined over $overline(bb(Q))$ in the rational Betti structure, because its idempotent has algebraic coefficients. Choose $0 eq.not x in H_eta^(upright("act"))$ and $0 eq.not u in U \( v \)_1 \( overline(bb(Q)) \)$. Define a $overline(bb(Q))$-linear map
  $ h : U \( v \)_(overline(bb(Q))) arrow.r H^1 \( S \, overline(bb(Q)) \) $
  by $h \( u \) = x$ and by setting it equal to zero on every other embedding line of $U \( v \)_(overline(bb(Q)))$. This is an element of
  $ "Hom"_(bb(Q)) #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\(] U \( v \) \, H^1 \( S \, bb(Q) \) #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\)] ⊗_(bb(Q)) overline(bb(Q)) . $
