== 7 Completion of the CM proof <sec:assembly>

The theta construction gives a nonzero period on a compact ball quotient. The finite-family extraction corollary expresses the one-form classes in that period through rational maps from the prescribed CM modules, after passage to sufficiently deep levels. We put these statements on one projective surface and apply the criterion of Section 3.

#proof[
  By Lemma 8, it suffices to treat the case $s gt.eq 2$ and $v_i \( 1 \) = 1$ for all four functions. Use the common Galois CM field $E$, the active embedding $mu = 1$, and the line signs
  $ d_i \( tau \) = v_i \( tau^(- 1) \) . $
  They satisfy $d_1 + d_2 = d_3 + d_4$ and $d_i \( mu \) = 1$. Choose the rank-three Hermitian space $V$, the ball $D$, and the rational orthogonal decomposition $W = W_1 perp W_2$ prescribed by $d_1 \, d_2$, as in Section 4.
  Proposition 16(ii) supplies a total finite theta input whose form for this decomposition is nonzero. With that input fixed, Corollary 17 supplies a second rational orthogonal decomposition and a nonzero mixed period. Write $X'$ for the individual-factor cover constructed there, and $xi_1 \, xi_2$ for the two pulled-back endpoint forms. On this common compact principal quotient they have finite expansions
  $ xi_1 = sum_(a in I) c_a thin Theta_1 \( phi.alt_(1 a) \) and Theta_2 \( phi.alt_(2 a) \) \, #h(2em) xi_2 = sum_(b in J) c'_b thin Theta_3 \( phi.alt_(3 b) \) and Theta_4 \( phi.alt_(4 b) \) \, $
  where the constants account for the chosen constant-line trivializations, and
  $ integral_(X') xi_1 and overline(xi_2) eq.not 0 . $
