  Apply Corollary 29 to these four families, with $X_(upright("base")) = X'$ and the fixed $E \, V \, D \, Lambda$. It gives a common smooth connected projective principal cover $pi : Y arrow.r X'$ on which all four $U \( v_i \)_1$-span conclusions hold; the auxiliary primes may differ.
  Denote the pulled-back one-form classes by
  $ theta.alt_(i a) = \[ pi^(*) Theta_i \( phi.alt_(i a) \) \] in H^1 \( Y \, bb(C) \) \, $
  with $a in I$ for $i = 1 \, 2$ and $a in J$ for $i = 3 \, 4$. These classes are represented by holomorphic one-forms. Their cup products compute the integrals of the wedge products, and the covering formula gives
  #[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(7.1)")
   $ 0 & eq.not integral_Y pi^(*) xi_1 and overline(pi^(*) xi_2)\
 & = sum_(a in I \, med b in J) c_a overline(c'_b) thin ⟨theta.alt_(1 a) union theta.alt_(2 a) union overline(theta.alt_(3 b)) union overline(theta.alt_(4 b)) \, \[ Y \]⟩ . $ <eq:assembly-period>]
  Choose $a \, b$ for which the displayed cup-product period is nonzero, and write its four holomorphic factors as $theta.alt_i$.
